{
  "summary": "This experiment isolated the effect of image encoder quality by replacing ResNet50 with ImageNet ViT-L in the otherwise identical multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool, weighted-fusion configuration (directly comparable to llm_summary_008). Validation accuracy rose from ~67.8% to ~70.6% (F1 from ~64.6% to ~66.7%), a ~2.8-point gain attributable to the encoder swap, indicating that the image branch was at least partially encoder-limited and that a stronger visual representation can amplify the complementary signal exploited by weighted fusion. It remains uncertain whether further encoder improvements, alternative image-branch aggregation, or different fusion mechanisms could push beyond ~70.6%, and whether the residual image contribution is now approaching a data-limited ceiling."
}

